hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20975","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us from Muadh ibn Rifah al-Ansari from a man from Banu Salamah called Sulaym who came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Muadh ibn Jabal comes to us after we sleep, and we are in our daytime works, and he calls for prayer, so we go out to him and he prolongs upon us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Muadh ibn Jabal, do not be a tempter. Either pray with me or lighten for your people. Then he said: O Sulaym, what have you of the Quran. He said: I ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge with Him from the Fire. By Allah, I do not do well your humming nor the humming of Muadh. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Does my humming and the humming of Muadh become but that we ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge with Him from the Fire. Then Sulaym said: You will see tomorrow when the people meet, God willing. He said: The people were preparing for Uhud, so he went out and was among the martyrs, the mercy of Allah and His pleasure upon him."
